Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Infiltrative lobular cancer of the left breast with positive margins in prior excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 NODES  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  WITH FLORID DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE OR IN SITU CARCINOMA  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Levine  REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm portion of tan pink fibrofatty tissue  which is sectioned to reveal hemorrhage and chalky yellow areas  consistent with fat necrosis  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lymph node  The lymph node is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also noted is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink lymph node  which is submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x 15 x 9cm left simple mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 12 5cm irregular tan portion of skin with a short black stitch designating the superior margin  and a long black stitch designating the axillary tail  There is an eccentric 4 4cm tan areola  which comes to 0 8cm of the closest superior skin margin  Centrally within the areola is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm flattened tan pink unremarkable nipple  Surrounding the areola along the lateral aspect is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm semicircular healed linear scar  which comes to 0 8cm of the closest superior skin margin  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm healed linear scar along the lateral skin  which comes to 0 5cm of the lateral skin margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  and the posterior black  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm exposed cavity along the mid posterior aspect  On sectioning  the cavity communicates with an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 4cm cavity  which is one half blood clot and one half cavity  This area comes to 0 3cm of the anterior margin and extends up to the scar on the skin surface adjacent to the areola  No residual tumor is grossly appreciated surrounding the cavity  Also noted in the upper outer quadrant is a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm region of chalky yellow discoloration  consistent with fat necrosis  The remainder of the specimen displays diffuse dense nodular gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals no apparent lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity  anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Region of fat necrosis in upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved mammary tissue  medial to cavity  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Lymph Nodes  Left Axilla   Dissection PART B  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Unchecked.
