Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 52 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  FORMING MANY NODULES THAT SPAN A REGION AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES WITH EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 24                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  g  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm unoriented left mastectomy specimen  which includes a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left axillary tail  and which is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 11 7cm skin ellipse  The skin ellipse includes a 5 5cm in diameter areola with central nipple  and a recent 4 0cm in length  healing scar  running 8 5cm superolateral to the nipple  The remainder of the skin is diffusely tan white and otherwise unremarkable  The deep resection margin is a smooth plane  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy site  characterized by sulfur yellow discoloration  located immediately subjacent to the epidermal incision  This biopsy cavity approaches to within 1 5cm of the superior margin  4 5cm of the deep inked margin  6 5cm of the inferior margin  and is distant from both the lateral and medial margins  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature  lobular  yellow  adipose tissue with thick  intercollating  fibrous bands  The axillary tail is explored for lymph nodes  Several lymph nodes are identified  Section Code  A  biopsy cavity with scar and superior margin  B  deep inked margin overlying biopsy site  C D  remainder of biopsy site  E G  fibrotic areas near biopsy site  H I  fibrosis at deep inked margin inferior to biopsy site  J  fibrosis at inferior margin  K  nipple  L O  low nodes  P Q  middle nodes  R  high nodes  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
