Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 58 CLINICAL DATA  History of breast cancer with xray therapy 15 yrs  ago  Aspirate showed spindle cell tumor                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT AND LEFT   BIOPSIES  MALIGNANT SPINDLE CELL NEOPLASM CONSISTENT WITH HIGH GRADE SARCOMA  BOTH SPECIMENS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunoperoxidase staining shows tumor cells positive for vimentin and antichymotrypsin and focally positive for keratin  EMA  and KP 1  CEA  desmin  smooth muscle actin  and S 100 stains are negative  The findings support the histological impression of sarcoma  EM results will be reported in an addendum  The frozen section diagnoses are confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 43                                                                                     ELECTRON MICROSCOPY Addendum          ELECTRON MICROSCOPY    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       RIGHT BREAST  FIBROSARCOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The neoplastic spindle cells have abundant cytoplasmic rough endoplasmic reticulum as their main feature  Some of these cells have focal collections of filaments with dense bodies  This ultrastructural picture is consistent with the cells being fibroblasts and myofibroblasts  and the diagnosis being fibrosarcoma or malignant fibrous histiocytoma  Added by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled  right breast  are two fragments of breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Specimens are inked and sectioned to reveal mottled waxy yellow tissue with areas of necrosis and areas of translucent gray tissue  Representative section frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Representative portions submitted for EM  Representative sections from larger fragment   The smaller sample is submitted in A and B  The larger sample entirely in C  D  and E  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  are multiple fragments of friable red tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in aggregate and REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm ellipse of skin excised to a depth of 1 5cm  The skin was inked and sectioned to reveal mottled yellow and grey translucent tissue  Representative section frozen as FX 2 and saved frozen  Skin fragments submitted in F and G  Friable red tissue in H  Gross Description by  ANTHONY FORRESTER  HMS Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 1  RIGHT BREAST   MALIGNANT SPINDLE CELL NEOPLASM  FAVOR SARCOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 2  SKIN AND SOFT TISSUE LEFT BREAST   ABUNDANT NECROSIS WITH ATYPICAL SPINDLE CELL PROLIFERATION  FAVOR SARCOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Horace C  Wu  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY PART B  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
