Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  30 AUG 94 at 12 37 CLINICAL DATA  52 year old female with infiltrating ductal carcinoma by breast biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SCAR AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE MATERIAL  FAT NECROSIS CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  NOTE The resection margins are free of tumor  Invasive carcinoma is not identified  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 04                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 20 x 12 x 4 5cm mastectomy with a 12cm in length by 3 to 5 x 2cm axillary tail  The overlying skin ellipse is 15 x 5cm  The nipple is 1 5cm  A 3cm well healed scar is present midway between the nipple and the lateral resection margin of the skin  1 to 2cm deep to the scar is white to tan  rubbery parenchyma intermixed with adipose tissue and focal hard white yellow speckled areas  Focal hemorrhage is present  Multiple small cysts less than 0 1cm are present  Some of the white rubbery tissue is slightly gritty  The closest resection margin is 0 5cm  The parenchyma lateral to the biopsy cavity is entirely fibrofatty tissue  Medial to the biopsy site  the tissue is largely adipose tissue with small streaks of thin fibrous tissue  Multiple small lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  Proximally  the nearest two nodes are 1cm in average dimension  Section Code  A B C  brea