in  4 0cm of the medial margin  6 0cm of the superior margin  and 9 0cm of the lateral margin  Additional sectioning of the breast parenchyma reveals a second prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm biopsy site consisting of intense stellate fibrosis and semifirm sulphur yellow discoloration  The biopsy site is immediately subjacent to the second epidermal scar located 1 5cm superomedial to the nipple  and approaches to within 1 0cm of the superior margin  2 5cm of the medial margin  2 5cm of the deep inked margin  5 3cm of the inferior margin  and 12 0cm of the lateral margin  A third REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm area of stellate fibrosis and sulphur yellow discoloration is located midway between the two biopsy sites  2 0cm deep to the nipple  and approaching to within 1 7cm of the superior margin  2 0cm of the deep inked margin  3 0cm of the medial margin  7 0cm of the inferior margin  and 11 5cm of the lateral margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature  lobular  yellow  adipose tissue with interculating fibrous bands  The axillary tail is explored for lymph nodes  eleven lymph nodes are identified in the upper one third of the tail  SECTION CODE  A E  inferior margin and skin  inferior biopsy   F G  superior margin and skin  superomedial biopsy   H  superior margin  fibrous area   I  deep inked margin  inferior biopsy   J  deep inked margin  superomedial biopsy   K  deep inked margin  fibrous area   L  medial margin  en face  M  lateral margin  en face  N  nipple  O T  lymph nodes  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
