ion Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  are two tan pink lymph nodes REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The nodes are entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1 2  now as cassettes A and B respectively  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan pink skin ellipse with an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm unremarkable tan pink nipple and well healed scar along the lateral edge  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm gray white  indurated  stellate firm area which comes to 0 3cm of the anterior  superficial  and 1 4cm of the deep margin  There is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm indurated  well defined  gray white lesion arising 5 5cm medial to the mass which comes to 0 4cm of the anterior  superficial  and 3 9cm of the deep margin  The remaining cut surface shows up to 40  focally gray white fibrotic tissue with cystic change  The remaining tan yellow and lobular adipose tissue demonstrates no other gross abnormalities  No lymph nodes are grossly identified  and representative sections are submitted as follows  C D  Firm area to superficial margin and skin  E F  Firm area to deep margin  G H  Firm area  I  Fibrous tissue adjacent to firm area  J  Second lesion  K L  Focally cystic dense fibrous tissue  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  DI TIAN  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA  O R  Diagnosis by  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PA