Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 55 CLINICAL DATA  Enhancing MRI area  MRI guided outside biopsy   LCIS                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  The prior specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   was reviewed  Dr  F  Koerner reviewed this case and agrees with this diagnosis  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 18 07                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm specimen of fibrofatty tissue with two localization needles through it  and a short stitch demarcating superior and a long stitch demarcating lateral as per the surgeon s note on the requisition form  The specimen is inked as follows  The superior surgical margin is inked blue  the inferior margin is inked black  the medial margin is inked green  and the lateral margin is inked in yellow  Serially sectioning from anterior to posterior reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 09cm solid tan pink mass in the center of the specimen grossly abutting the inferior and lateral margin  The mass is 0 2cm from the closest medial margin and 0 2cm from the closest superior margin  The mass is 0 3cm from the anterior pole of the specimen and 0 5cm from the posterior pole of the specimen  Sections of the mass and closest superior  inferior  medial and lateral margins are submitted in cassettes A E  The remainder of the specimen consisting of unremarkable tissue is submitted in cassettes F and G  Resident  CHRISTOPHER M  WILLIAM  MD   Ph D            