Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 12 CLINICAL DATA  Status post biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  1 RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  ADJACENT TO THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE   2 EXTENSIVE RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PRESENT ADJACENT TO  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN  NOTE  The margin of resection appears free of invasive and in situ carcinoma  3 METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 2 OF 19 LYMPH NODES    BREAST TISSUE   EXCISION   FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 45                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 22 x 16 x 2cm mastectomy specimen with a 13 x 5 5cm overlying  tan skin ellipse with a central  unremarkable nipple areolar complex  and a 3 2cm curvilinear sutured incision site 2 5cm from the superomedial aspect of the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned with over inking of the base of the biopsy cavity with blue ink  the base of the biopsy cavity was designated by the surgeon with four long silk sutures   Sectioning beneath the incision site reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm hemorrhagic  fragmented biopsy cavity  The biopsy cavity comes within 0 1cm of the deep resection margin  5 5cm from the closest superior margin  6 5cm from the closest inferior margin  3 5cm from the closest medial margin  and 13cm from the closest lateral margin  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm gritty area is adjacent to and inferior to the biopsy cavity which abuts the deep margin and is within 0 5cm of inferior margin  Remaining tissue is unremarkable fibrous breast tissue  SECTION CODE A B  Biopsy cavity in relation to deep margins  C  Biopsy cavity in relation to gritty lesion  D  Biopsy cavity in relation to skin  E  Hemorrhagic area of biopsy cavity  F  Representative section of gritty lesion with closest deep margin  G  Representative medial section  H  Representative lateral section with gritty nodularity  There is an attached 12 x 8 x 1 0cm axillary tail from which multiple lymph nodes are identified  The lymph nodes range in size from 0 3cm to 2 x 2 x 0 4cm in largest dimension  Representative sections from lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes I through N  Received in a separate container   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  breast tissue  is a 2 x 1 x 0 7cm unoriented piece of yellow tan fatty breast tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fatty tissue  Totally submitted in cassette O  Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST TISSUE , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 00 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  5 CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor grows as dispersed  small nests throughout a mass spanning five centimeters  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OF TEN LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The metastatic focus consists of a few cells in the subcapsular sinus  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm in greatest dimension  A skin ellipse with central nipple is attached with a long stitch at one end of the skin ellipse  and a short stitch ninety degrees away  The long stitch is parallel to an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm fibroadipose appendage to the bulk of the specimen  Two small fragments of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  6 0cm in greatest dimension are received  A central area of hard  irregularly outlined  white tan tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm in greatest dimension  0 9cm from the closest  deep  resection margin  The rest of the parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sections of the hard mass are in A E  Representative sections of adjacent areas of breast parenchyma are in F J  Ten lymph nodes from the  appendage  of the specimen parallel to the long stitch range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimensions  A section of each node is in K M  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 53 CLINICAL DATA  Large lobular carcinoma with lobular carcinoma in situ on outside biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA FORMING SEVERAL SMALL NODULES BOTH ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND AWAY FROM IT  IN SITU CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The in situ carcinoma exhibits a mixture of ductal and lobular characteristics  The invasive carcinoma forms several seemingly discrete nodules  making the size of the infiltrating component impossible to determine  The largest focus measures 0 4cm  and together the foci probably aggregate to about 1 0cm  Blood vessl and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  The tumor in the axillary lymph node spans about 0 3cm in greatest dimension in tissue section  and the cells extend into axillary fat  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number only is an 805 gram modified radical mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with an axillary tail REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm  At the central aspect of the inferior skin margin is a 2 5cm areola and nipple  and a healing scar is present 2 0cm in length extending to within 0 8cm to the superior margin and beginning 8 0cm from the medial margin of the skin ellipse  The specimen is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy cavity extending to within 0 7cm of the deep margin and to within 0 4cm of the superior margin  The remaining breast is unremarkable  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  A 0 5cm  hard  well circumscribed nodule is identified 3 0cm deep to the nipple  Section code  A D  biopsy site with deep margin E  biopsy site with superior margin F J  representative breast tissue K  well circumscribed nodule L  nipple M O  axillary lymph nodes Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  PART   RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
