Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 31 CLINICAL DATA  75 year old female with right breast segmentectomy  stitch on chest wall margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SEGMENTAL RESECTION  1 THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  2 BIOPSY CAVITY WITH ADJACENT FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  HISTIOCYTIC AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  3 SKIN SCAR  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA TO 1 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 57                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast segmentectomy  is an 8 x 8 x 6cm segmentectomy specimen containing a REMOVED_DATE x 1cm skin ellipse containing a 3cm well healed scar  No nipple is present  A single stitch designates the chest wall margin  posterior margin   A 5 5cm defect at the right margin leads into a 5 x 5 x 4cm biopsy cavity that extends to REMOVED_DATE to 0 8cm from most of the resection margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior margin is inked yellow  Sectioning reveals the biopsy cavity surrounded by fibrous tissue and white yellow opaque tissue  no grossly suspicious lesions are identified  Representative section of chest wall margin is frozen as frozen section  1  now A  representative sections of biopsy cavity submitted in B through K  with section containing skin in K  Labeled  Right axillary contents  is an 8 x 8 x 4cm mass of adipose tissue  containing approximately 20 lymph nodes measuring up to 2cm in greatest dimension  submitted entirely in L through O  Resident  EDWIN S  MO