ng in the medial half of the specimen which is consistent with previous biopsy site and comes to 0 5cm of the superficial  0 8cm of the inferior  1 0cm of the superior and deep  and 0 4cm of the medial margin  This region is also surrounded by yellow orange foci consistent with fat necrosis  The remaining cut surface is 20  tan yellow adipose and 80  dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as follows  A  Lateral margin  radially sectioned  B  Full thickness section including all margins from lateral half of the specimen  C  Cyst  D F  First hemorrhagic region to superior  inferior  superficial  and deep margins  G  Full thickness section including all margins to inferior aspect defect  G J  Second hemorrhagic area to superior  inferior  superficial  deep  and medial margins  with the medial margin radially sectioned as J  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  AQING   AHCHEAN   CHEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
