Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 09 50 CLINICAL DATA  50 year old female with infiltrating lobular carcinoma in the right breast biopsy with positive margins  Re excision and axillary dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA PRESENT IN SEVERAL APPARENTLY DISCRETE NODULES AND EXTENDING TO THE SUPERIOR OR INFERIOR MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN AT SEVERAL POINTS  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SMALL FOCUS   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The amount of the residual invasive carcinoma cannot be determined with accuracy  If aggregated  the foci of invasive carcinoma would probably form a mass about 1 2cm in greatest dimension in tissue section  Invasion of blood vessels or lymphatic vessels is not seen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 16 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES   HIGHEST AXILLARY NODE    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 16 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN   SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the corresponding values were 97  and 95   respectively  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 breast carcinomas with determination of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy nine percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 97  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  Right axillary nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 2 0cm specimen of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple soft tan lymph nodes  Lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes A and G  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  Highest axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 3cm soft tan lymph node submitted entirely in cassette H  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  Right breast reexcision stitch on deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 3 2cm specimen of soft white  tan  yellow tissue with a suture on one side and a REMOVED_DATE X 0 3cm attached skin ellipse  The specimen is doubled inked  yellow on the deep aspect  and in cross section reveals a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 1 2cm ill defined biopsy space that is composed of areas of soft white tan tissue and hemorrhage  Biopsy cavity is submitted entirely in cassette I through T  Resident  Jay Austen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  Lynn Arlene Weston  M D  PART A  AXILLARY NODES PART B  RE EXCISED RIGHT BREAST TISSUE PART C  HIGHEST AXILLARY NODE   report_end  , Unchecked.
