imen from medial to lateral with lateral margin having fibrous tissue adjacent to inferior border The smaller fragment of tissue  3 x 2 x 1cm  is inked where a suture was placed and radial sections are made  An ill defined tan red REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm area of tissue is identified extending to approximately 0 1cm from the inked surface  The entirety of the tissue is submitted in cassette M O  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  STEVEN GARDNER  MD PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 27 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEINS  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 97 at 17 06     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number only  are 5 cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  Angela Ann Giardino  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY , Unchecked.
