dominating in the inferomedial aspect  There is an area of dense fibrosis around the aforementioned cyst in the inferomedial aspect as well  No additional nodularity is noted  Attached to the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  from which multiple lymph nodes are identified  ranging from 0 5cm in greatest dimension  up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  SECTION CODE  A   Biopsy site scar  B D  Entire biopsy cavity in relation to closest superolateral margin  E G  Representative sections of cystic  fibrous regions from inferomedial regions  H K  Representative sections from each lymph node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal no discrete lesions and is entirely submitted in Cassettes L O  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional lateral margin   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  which are inked and sectioned to reveal no parenchymal abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted in Cassettes P S  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  RICHARD AMMER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCIS PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL MARGIN    EXCISI , Unchecked.
