Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 46 CLINICAL DATA  Re excision  right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  RE EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  RARE MICROSCOPIC FOCI  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE  SPANNING A REGION REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of invasive carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast  is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan to yellow soft tissue mass  with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse with 3 5cm centrally well healed scar  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy cavity surrounded by multiple areas of fibrofatty tissue and fat necrosis  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm white to grey  hard nodule 2 5cm from the biopsy cavity  There are surrounding firm white areas radiating from the nodule away from the skin and approaching and abutting the inked resection margin  The nodule is 1 0cm from the nearest resection margin  The biopsy cavity is 1 5cm from the nearest resection margin  SECTION CODE  A  skin ellipse  representative section B  suspicious nodule  representative section C D  suspicious tissue surrounding the nodule and abutting the resection margin  representative section E  biopsy cavity  representative section F J  remainder of suspicious nodule  ess  K  suspicious tissue under skin ellipse An X ray with needle localization accompanies the specimen  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 