renchyma  and biopsy sites and all the firmer areas are submitted in A through M  Labeled  Axillary nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with attached scant skeletal muscle  Multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 3cm are dissected from the adipose tissue  Only one of the lymph nodes has a focally white and firm cut surface  The other lymph nodes are grossly unremarkable  Representative half each lymph node are submitted in N through Q  the firmer lymph node in N   Labeled    base of biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Sectioning reveals grossly unremarkable adipose tissue with attached scant  fibrous tissue at one edge  representative two thirds of the specimen including all of the firmer areas are submitted in R through T  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Jay Solomon Markowitz  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  BASE  BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
