Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 32 CLINICAL DATA  69 year old women with left breast carcinoma  Long lateral suture  short superior                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  EXTENSIVE  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  MAMMARY CARCINOMA IN SITU  SMALL FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Infiltrating carcinoma involves many areas of the excision specimen  The foci of in situ carcinoma are small and distinction of lobular from ductal type is difficult  No definite vascular invasion is identified  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 07 49 Proofread by  RUBIN DANIEL                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 19     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 41     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Lumpectomy  short suture superior  long suture lateral  is a 13 x 10 x 5cm lumpectomy specimen with a 6 x 0 4cm overlying skin ellipse  A REMOVED_DATE x less than 0 1cm longitudinal healed scar is present running longitudinally along the center of the epidermal surface  A long and short suture are present on the skin ellipse designating lateral and superior orientation  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm firm  white  tan brown stellate region which is 2 5cm deep to the skin and which approaches to within 0 3cm of the nearest inked margin  The abnormal region is present midway between the medial and lateral aspect of the specimen  Section Code  A  skin with underlying unremarkable tissue  B I  brown  tan white stellate region  medial to lateral  J  fibrous tissue  lateral  K  unremarkable