t of the specimen  as per the surgeon  The specimen is inked for orientation as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm previous biopsy cavity within the lower inner quadrant at approximately the 9 o clock aspect of the specimen  The cavity focally abuts the anterior margin and is located 0 5cm from the posterior margin  The remaining cut surfaces consist of dense gray white fibrous tissue occupying approximately 60  of the cut surfaces  No discrete masses are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity  to include nearest posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and nearest anterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative lower outer breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative central breast  Received fresh  labeled  inferior medial margin left breast   are 3 fragments of fibroadipose tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The largest fragment is received with a suture designating the new margin  as per the surgeon  This aspect of the specimen is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining 2 fragments are sectioned and submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  each of which are dissected and palpated to reveal multiple candidate lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 4cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 candidate intact nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 candidate intact nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 candidate nodes  bisected  1 is inked black    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing 1 candidate bise