Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 58 CLINICAL DATA  47 year old woman with infiltrative and ductal carcinoma in situ of the left breast diagnosed by biopsy on REMOVED_DATE                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY     FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH EPITHELIOSIS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS     MULTIPLE PAPILLOMAS     RADIAL SCARS    MICROSCOPIC FIBROADENOMAS     SCAR WITH BIOPSY SITE     THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IN SITU OR INFILTRATIVE CARCINOMA     THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN FIFTEEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 33                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast and axillary nodes   is a 21 x 22 x 3cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 7 x 6 x 1cm axillary tail attached  An overlying skin ellipse measures 13 x 6cm  and a 2cm vertical biopsy incision site 2cm lateral to the areola is identified  The nipple is partially inverted  The specimen is incised through the previous biopsy site to reveal a portion of firm  white tissue 3cm deep to the skin margin  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved for receptor studies  The specimen is inked black  with a red stripe on the superior edge of the skin ellipse  and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm in greatest dimension previous biopsy site  The cut surface is notable for large areas of firm  gritty  white tan tissue abutting the anterior  superior and deep margins  which express milky white fluid  This entire area measures 13 x 12 x 3 2cm  SECTION CODE  A G  representative sections of firm  tan gray  gritty tissue in relation to deep margin  H  firm  tan  gritty tissue in relation to both deep and superior anterior margin   superior anterior with red dot of ink   I  firm tissue in relation to deep margin  J  representative section of breast parenchyma from lateral margin  K  representative section of breast parenchyma with ink on medial margin  L  representative section of firm  breast mass abutting superior anterior margin  M  representative section of skin ellipse with underlying breast parenchyma  N  nipple and areola  with underlying parenchyma  representative section  Located within the axillary fat are numerous semifirm to firm lymph nodes  measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm in diameter  Lymph nodes are submitted in O through U  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY    FOCAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  Douglas Brian Flieder  M D  PART   BREAST   AXILLARY NODES  LEFT  , Unchecked.
