Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 12 CLINICAL DATA  50 y o  female with carcinoma of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  FORMING SEVERAL NODULES ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND EXTENDING TO THE SUPERIOR AND INFERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The invasive carcinoma probably aggregates to less than 1 0cm  BREAST  RIGHT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 3 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  In 2 lymph nodes  the metastatic foci span less than 0 2cm  The tumor cells do not transgress the lymph node capsules  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast lumpectomy  is a oriented breast re excision specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm skin ellipse with a 2 0cm long well healed  oblique scar  The surgeon has denoted the superior aspect with a short stitch  and the lateral aspect with a long stitch  The superior half of the specimen is inked blue and the inferior half is inked black  Specimen is then sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic area abutting the deep resection margin  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm rubbery  firm white area abutting close to the inferior half of the specimen  A poorly demarcated  white  rubbery  firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lies at the deep aspect of the superior resection margin  This specimen is entirely submitted proceeding medially to laterally in cassettes A through E  with the described lesions in cassettes B  C and D  Received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right final shaved margins  are four fragments of focally cauterized fibroadipose tissue measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Since the specimen is received in four separate pieces  the specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely with the two smaller fragments in cassette F  the intermediate size fragment bisected in cassette G  the largest fragment serially sectioned in cassettes H and I  Received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of adipose tissue from which lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes J through P  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
